    <node id="Fixation monitoring">
      <data key="d0">Fixation monitoring</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A procedure that must be performed and recorded on the test to ensure subject compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-072f14c5d1083124-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-072f14c5d1083124</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761465</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="False-positive score">
      <data key="d0">False-positive score</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">A metric representing the percentage of incorrect positive results in a visual field test, which must not exceed 20 per cent for licensing reliability.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-072f14c5d1083124-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-072f14c5d1083124</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761465</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Visual field defect">
      <data key="d0">Visual field defect</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-072f14c5d1083124-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d2">Any person with a visual field defect or suspected of having one must undergo a formal perimetry-based assessment.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-072f14c5d1083124</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761465</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Visual field assessments">
      <data key="d0">Visual field assessments</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-072f14c5d1083124-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d2">This method serves as the minimum baseline standard for visual field assessments; if it shows no defect, the standard is confirmed.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-072f14c5d1083124</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761465</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Significant field defect">
      <data key="d0">Significant field defect</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-072f14c5d1083124-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d2">Subjects with a significant field defect or progressive eye condition require a binocular Esterman visual field for assessment.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-072f14c5d1083124</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761465</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Corrective lenses">
      <data key="d0">Corrective lenses</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-072f14c5d1083124-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-a09b64ac70a92828-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d2">The treating optometrist determines whether it is appropriate for a person to wear their normal corrective lenses during testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Eyewear used to improve vision and allow a person with suboptimal uncorrected visual acuity to meet driving standards.</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-072f14c5d1083124&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-a09b64ac70a92828</data>
