    <node id="Esterman binocular chart">
      <data key="d0">Esterman binocular chart</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-072f14c5d1083124-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d2">For an Esterman binocular chart to be considered reliable for licensing, the false-positive score must not exceed 20 per cent.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-072f14c5d1083124</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761465</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Diplopia">
      <data key="d0">Diplopia</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A visual condition characterized by double vision, excluding minor forms.&lt;SEP&gt;A condition characterized by double vision, excluding physiological diplopia.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical condition characterized by double vision, which is evaluated for its impact on driving fitness.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-0fe8bf8cdf4b51c6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-15bc1b265985cecd-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-007-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-0fe8bf8cdf4b51c6&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-15bc1b265985cecd&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-007</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761769</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Driving">
      <data key="d0">Driving</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The act of operating a vehicle, which individuals with significant diplopia are generally unfit to perform.&lt;SEP&gt;The activity that may be restricted due to progressive eye conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-0fe8bf8cdf4b51c6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-d60dc8429360a426-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-0fe8bf8cdf4b51c6&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-d60dc8429360a426</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761637</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Optometrist">
      <data key="d0">Optometrist</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A healthcare professional specializing in eye care who can assess patients experiencing diplopia.&lt;SEP&gt;A healthcare professional who recommends how lenses should be worn for orthokeratology therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;A healthcare professional who may refer a person for further assessment if they do not meet visual acuity standards.&lt;SEP&gt;A professional who assesses longstanding field defects for conditional licence consideration.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-0fe8bf8cdf4b51c6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-1fc74bd52e776429-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-550165120c8fdf79-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-0fe8bf8cdf4b51c6&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-1fc74bd52e776429&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-550165120c8fdf79&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761608</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ophthalmologist">
      <data key="d0">Ophthalmologist</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">An ophthalmologist is a medical doctor specializing in the diagnosis and treatment of eye diseases, serving as a key healthcare professional for assessing patients experiencing diplopia. This specialist evaluates eye health and vision to determine if an individual meets specific visual acuity standards or licensing requirements, often certifying a person's vision status according to established criteria.

In the context of driving, an ophthalmologist assesses longstanding field defects for conditional licence consideration and provides critical information regarding a driver's visual capabilities to the licensing authority. They recommend how lenses should be worn for orthokeratology therapy when necessary and may refer a person for further assessment if they do not meet required visual standards. Ultimately, this medical specialist plays a pivotal role in evaluating eye health and vision to ensure drivers satisfy the legal and safety prerequisites for operating a vehicle.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-0fe8bf8cdf4b51c6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-1fc74bd52e776429-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-550165120c8fdf79-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-a09b64ac70a92828-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-003-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-005-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-006-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-0fe8bf8cdf4b51c6&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-1fc74bd52e776429&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-550165120c8fdf79&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-a09b64ac70a92828&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-003&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-005&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-006</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761759</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Occluder">
      <data key="d0">Occluder</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A device used to manage diplopia by covering one eye, requiring a three-month non-driving period for re-establishment of depth perception.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-0fe8bf8cdf4b51c6-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-0fe8bf8cdf4b51c6</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761475</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Depth Perception">
      <data key="d0">Depth Perception</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The ability to perceive the world in three dimensions, which must be re-established after a non-driving period following diplopia management with an occluder.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-0fe8bf8cdf4b51c6-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-0fe8bf8cdf4b51c6</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761475</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Commercial Standards">
      <data key="d0">Commercial Standards</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Standards applicable to drivers of heavy vehicles, public passenger vehicles, or those requiring a dangerous goods driver licence.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761494</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Unconditional Licence">
      <data key="d0">Unconditional Licence</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A driving licence that is not subject to conditions based on visual fitness criteria.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of official permission or authorization that is subject to specific fitness criteria regarding vision.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of license that can be held by individuals meeting specific criteria, excluding those with visual field defects.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of driving licence that a person is not fit to hold if they are monocular.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of driving licence that can be held without specific restrictions, subject to fitness criteria.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-002-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-004-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-006-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-007-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-002&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-004&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-006&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-007</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761769</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Conditional Licence">
      <data key="d0">Conditional Licence</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Conditional Licence refers to a specialized form of driving authorization issued by the driver licensing authority, designed for both private and commercial vehicle operators who possess specific medical conditions affecting their vision. Unlike standard permits, this licence is granted subject to strict conditions and monitoring requirements that integrate the nature of the driving task with the individual's medical status, often necessitating adherence to particular visual acuity standards met through corrective measures such as orthokeratology therapy or regular use of lenses.

The administration of a Conditional Licence involves rigorous oversight mechanisms, typically requiring periodic review cycles ranging from annual to biennial intervals depending on the specific criteria and risk assessment. These reviews are not merely administrative but are critical for ensuring that the driver continues to meet the necessary visual benchmarks throughout their tenure. Consequently, the licence may be granted, modified, or revoked based on the outcomes of these evaluations, which serve as a dynamic feedback loop between the regulatory body and the driver's ongoing health status.

In essence, this permit represents a balanced approach to public safety and mobility, allowing individuals with specific visual impairments to operate vehicles while maintaining strict accountability through continuous medical monitoring and conditional restrictions tailored to their unique circumstances.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-1fc74bd52e776429-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-38541e18ac921ff2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-b9f8c41dbdf5f5ac-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-003-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-005-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-006-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-007-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-1fc74bd52e776429&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-38541e18ac921ff2&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-b9f8c41dbdf5f5ac&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-003&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-005&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-006&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-007</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761774</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Driver Licensing Authority">
      <data key="d0">Driver Licensing Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Driver Licensing Authority is the government body primarily responsible for evaluating, issuing, renewing, suspending, or cancelling a person's driver licence and conditional licence. This entity manages applications for conditional licences by assessing the nature of driving tasks in conjunction with specific medical conditions to determine eligibility. A core function involves reviewing driver fitness, which includes assessing patients with visual field defects based on established visual acuity standards.

Beyond routine licensing, the Authority handles exceptional cases by referring them for further medical specialist opinion when necessary. It is also tasked with reviewing conditional licences periodically; while some descriptions indicate an annual review cycle, others specify a two-year interval, suggesting a structured but potentially variable monitoring process depending on individual circumstances. Ultimately, the Driver Licensing Authority serves as the central authority ensuring that driving privileges are granted only to those who meet rigorous safety and medical requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-2bd3af88ef1410b0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-38541e18ac921ff2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-b9f8c41dbdf5f5ac-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-003-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-005-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-006-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-2bd3af88ef1410b0&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-38541e18ac921ff2&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-b9f8c41dbdf5f5ac&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-003&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-005&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-006</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761756</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Treating Optometrist">
      <data key="d0">Treating Optometrist</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A medical professional who provides information regarding a person's visual field to the licensing authority.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical professional who assesses and certifies visual acuity for driving license eligibility.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical professional who provides information regarding a driver's visual capabilities to the licensing authority.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical professional who provides information regarding a person's visual acuity and field to the driver licensing authority.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-003-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-005-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-006-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-003&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-005&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-006</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761752</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Treating Ophthalmologist">
      <data key="d0">Treating Ophthalmologist</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A medical professional who provides information regarding a person's visual field to the licensing authority.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761494</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Visual Field Defect">
      <data key="d0">Visual Field Defect</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Any defect in the visual field that renders a person unfit to hold an unconditional licence.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761494</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Binocular Visual Field">
      <data key="d0">Binocular Visual Field</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The combined visual field of both eyes, required to have an extent of at least 140 degrees within 10 degrees above and below the horizontal midline.&lt;SEP&gt;The extent of vision available to both eyes simultaneously, measured in degrees relative to the horizontal midline.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-005-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-005</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761737</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Scotoma">
      <data key="d0">Scotoma</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of significant visual field loss that may impede driving performance.&lt;SEP&gt;A localized area of visual field loss or blind spot.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-005-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-005</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761737</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hemianopia">
      <data key="d0">Hemianopia</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of significant visual field loss that may impede driving performance.&lt;SEP&gt;A condition characterized by loss of vision in one half of the visual field.&lt;SEP&gt;A condition characterized by the loss of vision in half of the visual field.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-005-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-005</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761737</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Quadrantanopia">
      <data key="d0">Quadrantanopia</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of significant visual field loss that may impede driving performance.&lt;SEP&gt;A condition characterized by loss of vision in one quarter of the visual field.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of visual field reduction resulting from neurological conditions or injuries.&lt;SEP&gt;A condition characterized by the loss of vision in one quarter of the visual field.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-005-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-005</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761737</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Visual Acuity">
      <data key="d0">Visual Acuity</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The sharpness of vision in the remaining eye, required to be 6/9 or better with or without correction for monocular drivers.&lt;SEP&gt;A person's clarity of vision, measured with or without glasses or contact lenses.&lt;SEP&gt;Visual acuity refers to the sharpness or clarity of vision, and evidence suggests that reduced levels increase motor vehicle crash risk, though this is challenging to identify precisely.&lt;SEP&gt;The sharpness of vision, a critical factor in detecting objects while driving.&lt;SEP&gt;A main aspect of vision being assessed in the chapter.&lt;SEP&gt;The measure of the sharpness of vision, specifically assessed in its uncorrected state for licensing purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;The sharpness of vision in the remaining eye, which must be 6/9 or better with or without correction.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-550165120c8fdf79-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-942a0e45a2a1e73d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-d9bb83d3b77476a5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-e2669d1b502303f5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-002-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-006-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-550165120c8fdf79&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-942a0e45a2a1e73d&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-d9bb83d3b77476a5&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-e2669d1b502303f5&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-002&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-006</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761756</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Monocular Vision">
      <data key="d0">Monocular Vision</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The state of having only one functional eye, which renders a person unfit to hold an unconditional licence.&lt;SEP&gt;The state of having vision with only one eye, resulting in reduced visual fields due to nasal obstruction and lack of stereoscopic vision.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761590</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Significant Visual Field Loss">
      <data key="d0">Significant Visual Field Loss</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-006-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d2">A person is not fit for a conditional licence if they have significant visual field loss (such as scotoma, hemianopia, or quadrantanopia) likely to impede driving performance.&lt;SEP&gt;For a conditional licence based on monocular vision, there must be no other significant visual field loss likely to impede driving performance.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761494</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Visual Field Loss">
      <data key="d0">Visual Field Loss</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-005-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d2">For a conditional licence based on binocular vision, the visual field loss must be static and unlikely to progress rapidly.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761494</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Visual Field">
      <data key="d0">Visual Field</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-006-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d2">For a conditional licence based on monocular vision, the visual field in the remaining eye must have a horizontal extent of at least 140 degrees within 10 degrees above and below the horizontal midline.&lt;SEP&gt;The extent of the area around a person that is visible at any one time, specifically requiring a horizontal extent of at least 140 degrees within 10 degrees above and below the horizontal midline.</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-117af1818c65d4ad&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-006</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761756</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Commercial standards">
      <data key="d0">Commercial standards</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Standards applicable to drivers of heavy vehicles, public passenger vehicles, or those requiring a dangerous goods driver licence.&lt;SEP&gt;A set of requirements for drivers of heavy vehicles, public passenger vehicles, or those requiring a dangerous goods driver licence.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-15bc1b265985cecd-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-a09b64ac70a92828-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-15bc1b265985cecd&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-a09b64ac70a92828</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761570</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Unconditional licence">
      <data key="d0">Unconditional licence</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of driving licence that can be held by a person who meets specific fitness criteria.&lt;SEP&gt;A driving licence that is held without conditions, subject to specific visual acuity limits for the holder.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-15bc1b265985cecd-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-a09b64ac70a92828-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-15bc1b265985cecd&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-a09b64ac70a92828</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761570</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Conditional licence">
      <data key="d0">Conditional licence</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of driving licence subject to conditions, which a person is not fit to hold if they experience certain visual impairments.&lt;SEP&gt;A driving licence that may be granted by the driver licensing authority subject to periodic review based on meeting specific visual standards.&lt;SEP&gt;A driving permit that requires assessment of visual field defects by an optometrist or ophthalmologist.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-15bc1b265985cecd-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-a09b64ac70a92828-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-15bc1b265985cecd&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-a09b64ac70a92828&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761608</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Physiological diplopia">
      <data key="d0">Physiological diplopia</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A form of diplopia that is considered normal or inherent and does not disqualify a person from holding a licence.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-15bc1b265985cecd-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-15bc1b265985cecd</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761503</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Central fixation">
      <data key="d0">Central fixation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The point in the visual field where an object is directly viewed, used as a reference for measuring diplopia.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-15bc1b265985cecd-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-15bc1b265985cecd</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761503</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Orthokeratology">
      <data key="d0">Orthokeratology</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A therapeutic approach involving the use of rigid gas-permeable contact lenses worn overnight to reshape the cornea of the eye.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-1fc74bd52e776429-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-1fc74bd52e776429</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761515</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Rigid Gas-Permeable Contact Lenses">
      <data key="d0">Rigid Gas-Permeable Contact Lenses</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Specialized contact lenses used in orthokeratology therapy that are worn overnight to reshape the cornea.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-1fc74bd52e776429-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-1fc74bd52e776429</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761515</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cornea">
      <data key="d0">Cornea</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The transparent front part of the eye that is reshaped by orthokeratology therapy.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-1fc74bd52e776429-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-1fc74bd52e776429</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761515</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Visual Refractive Error">
      <data key="d0">Visual Refractive Error</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A condition corrected by orthokeratology therapy, providing effective visual correction once the lenses are removed.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-1fc74bd52e776429-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-1fc74bd52e776429</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761515</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Private Vehicle Drivers">
      <data key="d0">Private Vehicle Drivers</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Individuals who may obtain a conditional licence to drive without normal correcting lenses if they meet visual acuity standards using orthokeratology therapy.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-1fc74bd52e776429-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-1fc74bd52e776429</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761515</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Commercial Vehicle Drivers">
      <data key="d0">Commercial Vehicle Drivers</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Individuals who may obtain a conditional licence to drive without normal correcting lenses if they meet visual acuity standards using orthokeratology therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Drivers operating trucks, buses, or other commercial vehicles who face no flexibility regarding visual field assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-1fc74bd52e776429-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-1fc74bd52e776429&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761590</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Medical Specialist Opinion">
      <data key="d0">Medical Specialist Opinion</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A formal assessment or recommendation provided by a medical specialist regarding an individual's condition or eligibility.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-2bd3af88ef1410b0-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-2bd3af88ef1410b0</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761520</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Part A section 3.3.7">
      <data key="d0">Part A section 3.3.7</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A specific section within Part A of the document that details the role of independent experts and panels.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-2bd3af88ef1410b0-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-2bd3af88ef1410b0</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761520</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Visual Acuity Standard">
      <data key="d0">Visual Acuity Standard</data>
      <data key="d1">standard</data>
      <data key="d2">A benchmark or requirement for clear vision that must be met for driving.&lt;SEP&gt;The required level of visual clarity that drivers with nystagmus must satisfy to be considered fit to drive.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-2be0d66af7c59510-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-849e8ea0a6b9fb07-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-2be0d66af7c59510&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-849e8ea0a6b9fb07</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761548</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Orthokeratology Therapy">
      <data key="d0">Orthokeratology Therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A therapeutic treatment used to maintain visual acuity standards.&lt;SEP&gt;A therapy used to meet the visual standard for a conditional license, as referenced in section 10.2.7.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-2be0d66af7c59510-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-003-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-2be0d66af7c59510&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-003</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761717</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Correcting Lenses">
      <data key="d0">Correcting Lenses</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Eyewear devices used to enable individuals to meet visual acuity standards when orthokeratology therapy is insufficient.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-2be0d66af7c59510-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-2be0d66af7c59510</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761524</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Health Professional">
      <data key="d0">Health Professional</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">An individual required to provide details of medical criteria not met, evidence of criteria met, proposed conditions, and monitoring requirements for the issuance of a conditional licence.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-38541e18ac921ff2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-38541e18ac921ff2</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761536</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Driver Licence">
      <data key="d0">Driver Licence</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A document that can be issued, renewed, suspended, or cancelled, including a conditional licence.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-38541e18ac921ff2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-38541e18ac921ff2</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761536</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Health">
      <data key="d0">Health</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A relevant factor considered in licensing decisions regarding fitness to drive.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-38541e18ac921ff2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-38541e18ac921ff2</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761536</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Driving Performance">
      <data key="d0">Driving Performance</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A relevant factor considered in licensing decisions regarding fitness to drive.&lt;SEP&gt;The ability to operate a vehicle safely and effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;The ability to operate a vehicle safely, which may be impeded by significant visual field loss.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-38541e18ac921ff2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-005-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-006-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-38541e18ac921ff2&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-005&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-VIS-COM-006</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761756</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Medical Criteria">
      <data key="d0">Medical Criteria</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Standards or requirements related to health that must be met for driving eligibility.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-38541e18ac921ff2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-38541e18ac921ff2</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761536</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hearing Impairment">
      <data key="d0">Hearing Impairment</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A medical condition that may affect fitness to drive when combined with other conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-38541e18ac921ff2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-38541e18ac921ff2</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761536</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Visual Impairment">
      <data key="d0">Visual Impairment</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A medical condition that may affect fitness to drive when combined with other conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-38541e18ac921ff2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-38541e18ac921ff2</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761536</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cognitive Impairment">
      <data key="d0">Cognitive Impairment</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A medical condition that may affect fitness to drive when combined with other conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-38541e18ac921ff2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-38541e18ac921ff2</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761536</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Older Drivers and Age-Related Changes">
      <data key="d0">Older Drivers and Age-Related Changes</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A section referenced regarding age-related factors affecting driving fitness.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-38541e18ac921ff2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-38541e18ac921ff2</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761536</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Multiple Medical Conditions">
      <data key="d0">Multiple Medical Conditions</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A section referenced regarding the combination of concurrent medical conditions affecting fitness to drive.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-38541e18ac921ff2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-38541e18ac921ff2</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761536</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fitness to Drive">
      <data key="d0">Fitness to Drive</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-38541e18ac921ff2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-db731186cdb786e3-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d2">Hearing impairment may combine with other medical conditions to affect fitness to drive.&lt;SEP&gt;The assessment of a person's ability and safety to operate a vehicle.</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-38541e18ac921ff2&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-db731186cdb786e3</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761668</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nystagmus">
      <data key="d0">Nystagmus</data>
      <data key="d1">condition</data>
      <data key="d2">A visual condition that may reduce visual acuity and requires assessment regarding fitness to drive.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-849e8ea0a6b9fb07-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-849e8ea0a6b9fb07</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761548</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Drivers">
      <data key="d0">Drivers</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Individuals who must meet specific visual acuity standards when they have nystagmus.&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals operating vehicles, categorized as either private or commercial, who are subject to potential standards regarding color vision.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-849e8ea0a6b9fb07-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-e8267bf4145306c0-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-849e8ea0a6b9fb07&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-e8267bf4145306c0</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761692</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Congenital Nystagmus">
      <data key="d0">Congenital Nystagmus</data>
      <data key="d1">condition</data>
      <data key="d2">A form of nystagmus present from birth, which may involve coping strategies compatible with safe driving.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-849e8ea0a6b9fb07-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-849e8ea0a6b9fb07</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761548</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Appropriate Specialist">
      <data key="d0">Appropriate Specialist</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A qualified professional who should conduct individual assessments for those with congenital nystagmus.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-849e8ea0a6b9fb07-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-849e8ea0a6b9fb07</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761548</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Visual Fields">
      <data key="d0">Visual Fields</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The visual field is a concept regarding the extent of space visible to an observer, which is noted as having incomplete evidence regarding its relationship to crash risk.&lt;SEP&gt;The extent of visual perception in all directions from the point of fixation, often affected by disorders of vision.&lt;SEP&gt;The extent of the area visible to an observer, important for detecting hazards.&lt;SEP&gt;A main aspect of vision being assessed in the chapter.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-942a0e45a2a1e73d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-cd83e305301149c8-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-d9bb83d3b77476a5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-e2669d1b502303f5-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-942a0e45a2a1e73d&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-cd83e305301149c8&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-d9bb83d3b77476a5&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-e2669d1b502303f5</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761677</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Motor Vehicle Crash Risk">
      <data key="d0">Motor Vehicle Crash Risk</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">This concept represents the likelihood of a vehicle accident, which is the primary outcome being investigated in relation to visual impairment factors.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-942a0e45a2a1e73d-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-942a0e45a2a1e73d</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761558</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Licensing Standards">
      <data key="d0">Licensing Standards</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">These are established criteria used to determine if a driver is legally permitted to operate a vehicle, and current evidence mostly covers drivers who already meet these standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-942a0e45a2a1e73d-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-942a0e45a2a1e73d</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761558</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Red Colour-Deficient Vision">
      <data key="d0">Red Colour-Deficient Vision</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A specific type of visual impairment characterized by difficulty distinguishing red colors, which presents challenges in detecting traffic signals like red lights.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-942a0e45a2a1e73d-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-942a0e45a2a1e73d</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761558</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Road Engineering">
      <data key="d0">Road Engineering</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Refers to the design and construction of roads and infrastructure, with significant improvements noted that may allow individuals with certain visual deficiencies to compensate while driving.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-942a0e45a2a1e73d-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-942a0e45a2a1e73d</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761558</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Driver licensing authority">
      <data key="d0">Driver licensing authority</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The governmental body responsible for evaluating and granting driving licences based on medical and visual criteria.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-a09b64ac70a92828-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-a09b64ac70a92828</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761570</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Visual acuity">
      <data key="d0">Visual acuity</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The clarity of vision measured as a ratio, such as 6/9 or 6/18, which determines fitness to hold certain types of driving licences.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-a09b64ac70a92828-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-a09b64ac70a92828</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761570</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Orthokeratology therapy">
      <data key="d0">Orthokeratology therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A treatment method referenced for meeting visual standards without corrective lenses, involving the use of contact lenses.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-a09b64ac70a92828-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-a09b64ac70a92828</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761570</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Central Loss">
      <data key="d0">Central Loss</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A visual field defect defined as an extension of hemianopia or quadrantanopia involving more than three missed points.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761590</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Real-World Driving Environment">
      <data key="d0">Real-World Driving Environment</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The practical context of driving where drivers move their eyes freely and operate under variable conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761590</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Kinetic Fields">
      <data key="d0">Kinetic Fields</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A method of measuring visual fields conducted on a Goldman device.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761590</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Esterman Visual Fields">
      <data key="d0">Esterman Visual Fields</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A method of measuring visual fields that can be conducted binocularly without fixation monitoring, often referred to as roving Esterman.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761590</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Roving Esterman">
      <data key="d0">Roving Esterman</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A specific type of Esterman visual field test requiring two consecutive tests with no more than one false-positive allowed.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761590</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Numeric Field Format">
      <data key="d0">Numeric Field Format</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">The format in which roving Esterman visual fields should be printed or sent for an opinion.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761590</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Contrast Sensitivity">
      <data key="d0">Contrast Sensitivity</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A factor considered by driver licensing authorities when assessing patients with visual field defects.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761590</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Glare Susceptibility">
      <data key="d0">Glare Susceptibility</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A factor considered by driver licensing authorities when assessing patients with visual field defects.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761590</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Medical History">
      <data key="d0">Medical History</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Information regarding the duration and prognosis of a condition, whether it is progressive, the rate of progression or deterioration, and the effectiveness of treatment or management.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761590</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Driving Record">
      <data key="d0">Driving Record</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">The history of driving behavior before and after the occurrence of a visual defect.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761590</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nature of Driving Task">
      <data key="d0">Nature of Driving Task</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Factors such as vehicle type, road conditions, distances to be travelled, and concomitant medical conditions like cognitive impairment or neck rotation issues.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-a5934e81e0aee450</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761590</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Visual fields">
      <data key="d0">Visual fields</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A measure of the extent of peripheral (side) vision used for assessing driving awareness and safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761608</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Normal visual field">
      <data key="d0">Normal visual field</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Defined as 60 degrees nasally, 100 degrees temporally, 75 degrees inferiorly, and 60 degrees superiorly.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761608</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Binocular field">
      <data key="d0">Binocular field</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Extends the horizontal extent from 160 to 200 degrees, with a central 120 degrees overlapping for stereopsis.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761608</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stroke">
      <data key="d0">Stroke</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A neurological condition that can reduce visual fields.&lt;SEP&gt;A neurological condition where vision is one of several functional outcomes assessed for driving fitness.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-db731186cdb786e3-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-db731186cdb786e3</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761668</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Multiple sclerosis">
      <data key="d0">Multiple sclerosis</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A neurological condition that can reduce visual fields.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761608</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Glaucoma">
      <data key="d0">Glaucoma</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">An ocular disease that can reduce visual fields.&lt;SEP&gt;An example of a progressive eye condition mentioned in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;A progressive eye condition that is more common in older people and requires regular monitoring for driving.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-d60dc8429360a426-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-db731186cdb786e3-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-d60dc8429360a426&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-db731186cdb786e3</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761668</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hemionopia">
      <data key="d0">Hemionopia</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of visual field reduction resulting from neurological conditions or injuries.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761608</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Monocularity">
      <data key="d0">Monocularity</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of visual field reduction resulting from neurological conditions or injuries.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761608</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fovea area">
      <data key="d0">Fovea area</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The central part of the eye where information is identified after being alerted by peripheral vision.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761608</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Driver">
      <data key="d0">Driver</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d2">Assists the driver in being aware of the total driving environment before central focus is applied.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761608</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Peripheral vision">
      <data key="d0">Peripheral vision</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d2">Assists the driver in being aware of the total driving environment before central focus is applied.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761608</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Peripheral vision loss">
      <data key="d0">Peripheral vision loss</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d2">Incomplete peripheral vision loss allows awareness through adaptation, while full impairment decreases safety.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761608</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Farmer">
      <data key="d0">Farmer</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">An individual requiring a commercial vehicle licence for the occasional use of a heavy vehicle.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-b9f8c41dbdf5f5ac-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-b9f8c41dbdf5f5ac</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761618</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Interstate Multiple Combination Vehicle Driver">
      <data key="d0">Interstate Multiple Combination Vehicle Driver</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A driver whose licence status differs from that of a farmer due to the nature of their driving task.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-b9f8c41dbdf5f5ac-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-b9f8c41dbdf5f5ac</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761618</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Examining Health Professional">
      <data key="d0">Examining Health Professional</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The professional responsible for examining persons and providing advice to the driver licensing authority regarding medical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-b9f8c41dbdf5f5ac-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-b9f8c41dbdf5f5ac</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761618</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Patient">
      <data key="d0">Patient</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">An individual whose condition may affect their ability to drive and who has a legal obligation to notify authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">AFTD2022-EXP-b9f8c41dbdf5f5ac-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;AFTD2022-EXP-d60dc8429360a426-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">AFTD2022-EXP-b9f8c41dbdf5f5ac</data>
      <data key="d5">1792761618</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Practical Driver Assessment">
