      <data key="d12">1792761475</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Diplopia" target="Commercial standards">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Experiencing diplopia (other than physiological diplopia) within 20 degrees from central fixation is a criterion for determining if a person is not fit to hold certain licences.</data>
      <data key="d9">disqualification,visual impairment</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-15bc1b265985cecd-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-15bc1b265985cecd</data>
      <data key="d12">1792761503</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Diplopia" target="Physiological diplopia">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Physiological diplopia is excluded from the definition of diplopia that renders a person unfit to hold a licence.</data>
      <data key="d9">exclusion,normal vision</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-15bc1b265985cecd-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-15bc1b265985cecd</data>
      <data key="d12">1792761503</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Diplopia" target="Physiological Diplopia">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The condition of experiencing diplopia is relevant to licence fitness unless it is classified as physiological diplopia.</data>
      <data key="d9">classification,exception,exclusion</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-VIS-COM-007-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-VIS-COM-007</data>
      <data key="d12">1792761774</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Diplopia" target="Central Fixation">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The assessment of diplopia involves measuring its presence within 20 degrees from the point of central fixation.</data>
      <data key="d9">measurement,range,visual field</data>
