      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Fitness to Drive" target="Vision">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The state of vision is a critical consideration when assessing an individual's fitness to drive.</data>
      <data key="d9">assessment,safety</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-db731186cdb786e3-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-db731186cdb786e3</data>
      <data key="d12">1792761668</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Fitness to Drive" target="Older People">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">For older people, fitness to drive involves considerations of vision alongside cognition and sensory-motor function.</data>
      <data key="d9">assessment,factors</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-db731186cdb786e3-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-db731186cdb786e3</data>
      <data key="d12">1792761668</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Fitness to Drive" target="Stroke">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">For drivers with stroke, vision is one of the functional outcomes addressed in an overall assessment of fitness to drive.</data>
      <data key="d9">assessment,outcome</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-db731186cdb786e3-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-db731186cdb786e3</data>
      <data key="d12">1792761668</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Fitness to Drive" target="Neurological Conditions">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Findings related to neurological conditions such as stroke are integrated as part of the overall assessment for fitness to drive.</data>
      <data key="d9">assessment,integration</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-db731186cdb786e3-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-db731186cdb786e3</data>
      <data key="d12">1792761668</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Nystagmus" target="Appropriate Specialist">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Individuals with nystagmus should be assessed by an appropriate specialist to determine fitness to drive.</data>
      <data key="d9">assessment,evaluation,medical review</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-849e8ea0a6b9fb07-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-849e8ea0a6b9fb07</data>
      <data key="d12">1792761548</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Drivers" target="Doctors">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Medical professionals should advise drivers who have significant color vision deficiency about the impact on their driving.</data>
      <data key="d9">advice,deficiency,medical guidance</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-e8267bf4145306c0-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-e8267bf4145306c0</data>
      <data key="d12">1792761692</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Drivers" target="Optometrists">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Eye care specialists should inform drivers regarding how color vision deficiency affects responsiveness to signal lights and the need for driving adaptations.</data>
      <data key="d9">adaptation,advice,visual impairment</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-e8267bf4145306c0-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-e8267bf4145306c0</data>
      <data key="d12">1792761692</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Drivers" target="Ophthalmologists">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Eye specialists should advise drivers on how color vision deficiency impacts their ability to respond to signal lights and the necessity of adapting their driving.</data>
      <data key="d9">adaptation,advice,visual impairment</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-e8267bf4145306c0-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-e8267bf4145306c0</data>
      <data key="d12">1792761692</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Drivers" target="Signal Lights">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Drivers must respond to signal lights, a task that can be affected by significant color vision deficiency.</data>
      <data key="d9">perception,responsiveness,traffic signals</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-e8267bf4145306c0-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-e8267bf4145306c0</data>
      <data key="d12">1792761692</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Drivers" target="Colour Vision">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">There is currently no established standard for colour vision requirements applicable to drivers in either private or commercial contexts.</data>
      <data key="d9">absence,requirement,standard</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-e8267bf4145306c0-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-e8267bf4145306c0</data>
      <data key="d12">1792761692</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Congenital Nystagmus" target="Appropriate Specialist">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Those with congenital nystagmus may have developed coping strategies and require individual assessment by a specialist.</data>
      <data key="d9">assessment,coping strategies,individual evaluation</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-849e8ea0a6b9fb07-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-849e8ea0a6b9fb07</data>
      <data key="d12">1792761548</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Visual Fields" target="Motor Vehicle Crash Risk">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">There is an incomplete relationship between visual fields and crash risk, as the evidence regarding this association is limited.</data>
      <data key="d9">association,evidence,safety</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-942a0e45a2a1e73d-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-942a0e45a2a1e73d</data>
      <data key="d12">1792761558</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Visual Fields" target="Practical Driver Assessment">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The practical driver assessment is not considered a safe or reliable method for assessing the effects of disorders of vision on visual fields.</data>
      <data key="d9">assessment,limitations</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-cd83e305301149c8-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-cd83e305301149c8</data>
      <data key="d12">1792761628</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Motor Vehicle Crash Risk" target="Red Colour-Deficient Vision">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Research suggests there is no general association between crash risk and colour vision, though individuals with red-colour-deficient vision have difficulty detecting red lights in laboratory and on-road testing.</data>
      <data key="d9">colour vision,laboratory testing,red lights</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-942a0e45a2a1e73d-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-942a0e45a2a1e73d</data>
      <data key="d12">1792761558</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Red Colour-Deficient Vision" target="Road Engineering">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Significant improvements in road engineering mean that people with red-colour-deficient vision may largely compensate for their deficiency while driving.</data>
      <data key="d9">compensation,driving capability,engineering improvements</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-942a0e45a2a1e73d-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-942a0e45a2a1e73d</data>
      <data key="d12">1792761558</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Driver licensing authority" target="Orthokeratology therapy">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The driver licensing authority refers to Orthokeratology therapy for information on meeting the visual standard using this specific treatment.</data>
      <data key="d9">information,reference,standards</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-a09b64ac70a92828-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-a09b64ac70a92828</data>
      <data key="d12">1792761570</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Visual fields" target="Normal visual field">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Defines the extent of normal peripheral vision in terms of degrees in different directions.</data>
      <data key="d9">definition,measurement</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023</data>
      <data key="d12">1792761608</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Visual fields" target="Binocular field">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Extends the horizontal visual range and provides overlapping central vision for depth perception.</data>
      <data key="d9">extension,stereopsis</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023</data>
      <data key="d12">1792761608</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Visual fields" target="Stroke">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">A neurological condition that can cause a reduction in the extent of visual fields.</data>
      <data key="d9">neurological condition,reduction</data>
      <data key="d10">AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d11">AFTD2022-EXP-adb72bb1f206f023</data>
      <data key="d12">1792761608</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Visual fields" target="Multiple sclerosis">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">A neurological condition that can cause a reduction in the extent of visual fields.</data>
      <data key="d9">neurological condition,reduction</data>
